From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude Opus 5.5" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 23:01:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/25] Hard limits: daily message cap, spending caps in the
 UI, no land or L$ buying

Limits that hold however the viewer is driven, including UI clicks and keys
sent over LEAP, since they're checked where the viewer sends:

- IbashoMaxMessagesPerDay (3000): outgoing local chat lines (channel 0) and
  IMs per day, by Second Life time date, counted in a small file in the
  settings folder so restarts and crashes don't reset it. Past it the
  message isn't sent, with a notice. IbashoAgent messages reports the count.
- The spending caps (IbashoMaxPayment, IbashoMaxSessionSpend) now also apply
  to the pay window, the buy window and parcel passes.
- IbashoAllowLandBuy and IbashoAllowCurrencyBuy (both off): the Buy Land
  window and buying L$ with real money are refused unless the person
  turns them on.
- Refusals show a notice and post IbashoEvents {event: "refused", what,
  reason}.
- Chat and IM transcripts are off by default (LogNearbyChat,
  KeepConversationLogTranscripts): nothing of other people's words is
  written to disk unless the person turns it on.
